{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed: Gerrit 3426 merged to main as 9d205edbd45fc9aad76538f5e6e9a19ab5f5200e (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments). All 6 acceptance criteria checked against origin/main: AGENTS.md's PPID 1 bullet names compact_trigger, gc_trigger and _store.push; docs/orphaned-processes.md names all 3, says to leave them, calls the sweep safe to interrupt and prefers SIGTERM; scripts/check_orphaned_load.py has is_rebar_detached_worker and the \"rebar detached worker\" report label; tests/unit/test_orphaned_processes_guidance.py has test_guidance_names_every_spawn_detached_worker.\n\nWindows sweep: not needed. The change touches only guidance text, a pure string matcher over `ps` command-line text, and tests that inject records and spawn no process. It adds no subprocess, fd, path, encoding or permission handling, so it has nothing Windows-specific to break. (A Windows sweep is being dispatched anyway for the A1 stack after it lands; its result will cover main at that point.)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795040596611931876,"uuid":"e76f9719-350e-4b6e-b756-6d8018ad056a"}